$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure A for the synthesis of
substrate (1): 1 To a Schlenk tube (50-mL) were added Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (70
mg, 0.1 mmol, 2 mol %), K3PO4·nH2O (1.73 g, 7.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv) and
substrate 3 (5 mmol, 1.0 equiv). The mixture was closed by a septum,
purged by nitrogen gas for several times then the dry toluene (20 mL) was
slowly injected into the mixture by a syringe and the mixture was allowed
to stir for 10 min; o-bromoiodoarene 4 (7.5 mmol) was then slowly
injected into the mixture by a syringe. The septum was removed and the
Schlenk tube was sealed with cap; again quickly purged by nitrogen gas
for several times and move to oil bath and allowed to stir at 100 °C for
12 h. The crude reaction mixture was diluted with 30 mL CH2Cl2, filtered
through a thin Celite pad to remove salt and concentrated in vacuo. The
residue was isolated through column chromatography by using hexane and
ethyl acetate as eluent. Compounds 1. Compounds 1a–1o, 1A–1F and 1H–1J
were obtained according to this procedure.
2'-Bromo-[1,1'-biphenyl]-2-carbonitrile (1a): According to the general
procedure A, Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (70 mg, 0.1 mmol, 2 mol %), K3PO4·nH2O (1.73 g,
7.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), 2-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-
1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)benzonitrile (1.15 g, 5 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and
o-bromoiodobenzene (1.69 g, 6.0 mmol, 1.2 equiv) were stirred in dry
toluene (20 mL) at 100 °C for 2 h. Work-up and purification by column
chromatography (Hex/EtOAc = 19:1).
2'-Fluoro-[1,1'-biphenyl]-2-carbonitrile (1aa): According to the general
procedure A, Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (70 mg, 0.1 mmol, 2 mol %), K3PO4·nH2OH2O (1.73
g, 7.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), 2-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-
1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)benzonitrile (1.15 g, 5 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and
o-fluoroiodobenzene (1.33 g, 6.0 mmol, 1.2 equiv) were stirred in dry
toluene (20 mL) at 100 °C for 3 h. Work-up and purification by column
chromatography (Hex/EtOAc = 97:3). Product 1aa as a white solid (729 mg,
74%). Registry Number: [400820-15-7]. mp: 80–81 °C; IR (KBr): 2926, 2229,
1635, 1216, 758 cm-1;1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.78 (dd, J = 7.8 Hz, 0.6
Hz, 1H), 7.66 (td, J = 7.8, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.52–7.46 (m, 2H), 7.45–7.41 (m,
2H), 7.28–7.20 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3): δ 159.4 (d, J = 246
Hz), 139.6, 133.2, 132.5, 131.2, 131.0, 130.8, 128.2, 125.8 (d, J = 15
Hz), 124.4 (d, J = 3 Hz), 118.0, 116.1 (d, J = 23 Hz), 112.8; HRMS (EI+):
197.0643 (cal. for C13H8FN 197.0641).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, slow additions of toluene stage 1 and arene stage 2,
sealed tube used (Schlenk), Suzuki coupling
